.SH KEYS
In the dashboard, \fB?\fR lists every key, and \fB?\fR again explains every word and number on screen. \fBq\fR quits and restores the terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The program ran and ended normally. This says nothing about the network, unless \fB\-\-assert\fR was given.
.TP
.B 1
An unexpected internal error.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an option that cannot be understood, an assertion that could never be checked, or an interactive command without a terminal.
.TP
.B 3
The configuration is invalid. Every problem is listed.
.TP
.B 4
No stream could be started: every configured probe is unsupported or refused on this host.
.TP
.B 5
An error on an output that was asked for: a recording, an export, or records written to a pipe that closed before an asserted sample was complete.
.TP
.B 10
A \fBsample \-\-assert\fR check was false, or could not be evaluated.
.TP
.B 130, 143
Ended by SIGINT or SIGTERM in a headless command.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PATHWATCH_CONFIG
The configuration file, when \fB\-\-config\fR is not given.
.TP
.B PATHWATCH_NEXTDNS_PROFILE
Your NextDNS profile id. It is masked on screen and removed from recordings as they are written.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When not empty, no colour is used. Bold and reverse video are kept.
.TP
.B COLORTERM, TERM
How many colours the terminal has.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, HOME
Where the default configuration file and the recording directory are looked for.
.TP
.B HTTPS_PROXY, ALL_PROXY
Noticed and reported. DNS over HTTPS connects to the resolver itself and does not use a proxy.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pathwatch/config.toml
The configuration file, if it exists. \fBpathwatch config path\fR says which file is in use, \fBpathwatch config example\fR prints a commented one, and \fBpathwatch config reference\fR explains every setting.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/pathwatch/recordings/
Recordings, one directory per session, when recording is asked for.
.SH NOTES
On Linux, ICMP needs \fInet.ipv4.ping_group_range\fR to include one of your groups. Where it does not, ICMP streams are reported as unsupported with the remedy, and everything else runs. \fBpathwatch doctor\fR reports what the host permits, and sends nothing.
.PP
\(lqno\-reply\(rq is the share of probes that got no answer. It is not proof of packet loss on your line. \fBpathwatch glossary\fR explains every term.
